# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Line endings: do not touch them, ever.
#
# This repo is worked on from Windows (STM32CubeIDE, PowerShell) and from WSL.
# Git for Windows defaults to core.autocrlf=true and rewrites files to CRLF on
# checkout; WSL git usually has it false. With no rules here, each side sees the
# other's line endings as an edit to every line of every file, and `git pull`
# fails with "cannot pull with rebase: You have unstaged changes" over 300 files
# nobody touched.
#
# `-text` disables all conversion: the bytes in your working tree are exactly the
# bytes in the commit, on every platform. That is also what this repo needs for a
# second reason — it is a consolidation of teammates' work committed unmodified,
# and normalising line endings would silently rewrite every one of those files.
#
# This overrides core.autocrlf, so it works without anyone reconfiguring git.
* -text
